The '''2026 Seattle Storm season''' was the 27th season for the [[Seattle Storm]] of the [[Women's National Basketball Association]] and their first under head coach [[Sonia Raman]]. The Storm failed to qualify for the playoffs and finished at the bottom of the league standings, with 8 wins and 36 losses—the worst record in franchise history.<ref>{{cite news |last=Allen |first=Percy |date=September 23, 2026 |title=Seattle Storm close worst season in franchise history with loss to Dallas Wings |url=https://www.seattletimes.com/sports/storm/seattle-storm-close-worst-season-in-franchise-history-with-loss-to-dallas-wings/ |work=[[The Seattle Times]] |accessdate=October 2, 2026}}</ref> The team also set the record for most losses in an WNBA season.<ref>{{cite news |last=Allen |first=Percy |date=September 20, 2026 |title=Seattle Storm fall to Aces, set WNBA record for most losses in a season |url=https://www.seattletimes.com/sports/storm/seattle-storm-fall-to-aces-set-wnba-record-for-most-losses-in-a-season/ |work=The Seattle Times |accessdate=October 2, 2026}}</ref>

